.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt GATES 7
.Os ELSEWHERE
.Sh NAME
.Nm gates ,
.Nm foreign-lint ,
.Nm mk-lint ,
.Nm banned-lint ,
.Nm want
.Nd the kit's checks of foreign material, Makefiles and banned calls
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm foreign-lint
.Ar root
.Nm mk-lint
.Ar root
.Nm banned-lint
.Ar root
.Nm want
.Op Fl l Ar law
.Ar status
.Ar command
.Op Ar arg ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A gate reads a tree and decides one mechanical question about it.
Each is a script that
.Xr sh 1
runs from the gates directory, as in
.Ic sh gates/mk-lint root .
The kit keeps three:
.Bl -tag -width banned-lint
.It Nm foreign-lint
material that the foundation keeps out of kit inputs (STANDARDS section 1)
and shell that is not
.Pa /bin/sh
with base tools (section 6);
.It Nm mk-lint
Makefiles without a real
.Cm check
target (sections 3 and 6), and builds that weaken the C99 flags or the
allocator (section 4);
.It Nm banned-lint
calls to C library routines that copy or format without a bound, run a
shell or convert without an error check (section 4).
.El
.Pp
Each gate walks every regular file under
.Ar root ,
judges the files of the kinds it knows, prints each finding on standard
output and one summary line on standard error.
A finding is one line of four fields separated by tabs:
the law, the file, the line number (0 when the finding has none) and the
reason.
.Ss Results
.Bl -tag -width UNKNOWN
.It PASS
The gate judged at least one file and found nothing.
This is bounded evidence about the judged files and the listed laws only.
.It FAIL
At least one finding.
A finding is reported even when other files are UNKNOWN, and those stay
visible in the output.
.It UNKNOWN
The gate could not decide: the walk was refused, a tool failed, no file
of a judged kind was found, or a construct cannot be decided statically.
UNKNOWN is never PASS.
.El
.Ss The walk
Every gate walks
.Ar root
with
.Pa walk ,
which refuses the whole walk, and so makes the gate UNKNOWN, when
.Ar root
is missing or starts with
.Ql - ,
when any name under it holds a byte outside
.Ql "A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ + -" ,
or when a symbolic link or special file is under it.
Directories named
.Pa .got
or
.Pa .git
are not walked.
.Pp
A directory listed in
.Pa root/GATE-FIXTURES
holds deliberate violations, such as these controls, and is not walked.
Each line is empty, a comment starting with
.Ql # ,
or one relative directory path in the name alphabet with no
.Ql \&.
or
.Ql ..
step, with a step named
.Pa controls
or
.Pa tests ,
naming an existing directory.
Any other line refuses the walk, so the list cannot quietly widen.
.Ss foreign-lint laws
.Bl -tag -width NO-GNU-MAKE
.It NO-LINUX
in C, a Linux-only header such as
.In sys/epoll.h
or a token such as
.Dv __linux__
or
.Dv _GNU_SOURCE .
.It NO-GNU-C
in C, a GNU extension that
.Fl std=c99 Fl Wpedantic
lets through:
.Dv __attribute__ ,
.Dv __typeof__ ,
.Dv __builtin_* ,
.Dv __extension__ ,
.Dv __asm__
or
.Ql asm( .
.It NO-GNU-MAKE
in a Makefile, a GNU conditional, function, pattern rule or directive.
.It POSIX-SH
in a shell script, an interpreter other than
.Pa /bin/sh ,
or a bashism:
.Ql [[ ,
a here-string, an array, a bash builtin, a bash substitution,
.Ql $'...'
or
.Ic source .
.It NO-GNU-TOOL
in a script or Makefile,
.Ic sha256sum ,
.Ic sha1sum ,
.Ic md5sum ,
.Ic tac ,
.Ic stat -c ,
.Ic find -printf ,
.Ic grep -P
or
.Ic date -d .
.It C99-FLAGS
in a script or Makefile, a
.Fl std
setting that is not
.Cm c99 .
.It NO-GIT
a git metadata file, a
.Pa .git
directory, or a command that runs git.
.It PYTHON
a Python file, or a script or Makefile that runs Python.
Python is the third tier and needs a written reason (STANDARDS section 1).
.El
.Pp
A C file is judged with its comments removed; a shell script or Makefile
is judged without its comment lines.
.Ss mk-lint laws
Every file named
.Pa Makefile ,
.Pa makefile
or
.Pa BSDmakefile
is judged together with the files it includes.
A quoted include is followed relative to the including file;
.Ql <file>
is the system's and is not followed.
.Bl -tag -width NOCHECK
.It NOCHECK
no target named
.Cm check .
.It EMPTY
a target named
.Cm check
or
.Cm test ,
or starting with
.Cm check-
or
.Cm test- ,
or ending with
.Cm -check
or
.Cm -test ,
that executes nothing: its recipe is empty or holds only comments, bare
continuations,
.Ql \&: ,
.Ic true ,
.Ic exit 0 ,
or an
.Ic echo
or
.Ic printf
that pipes, redirects and substitutes nothing.
An empty recipe whose prerequisites include such a target delegates, and
is not EMPTY.
.It FLAGS
C is built (a
.Pa .c
operand,
.Va ${CC}
or
.Pa bsd.prog.mk )
but no
.Va CFLAGS
line carries
.Fl std=c99 Fl Wall Fl Wextra Fl Wpedantic Fl Werror ;
or
.Va CFLAGS
is replaced without them; or it is set with
.Ql ?= ,
which has no effect after
.Pa sys.mk
defines it.
.It WEAKEN
an option
.Fl Wno-* ,
.Fl w
or
.Fl fpermissive .
.It CC
.Va CC
set to anything but
.Ic cc .
.It MALLOC
.Ev MALLOC_OPTIONS
named other than as
.Ql MALLOC_OPTIONS=S .
.El
.Pp
A target or prerequisite spelled through a variable, an include spelled
through a variable when no
.Cm check
target is seen, a missing include, an include outside
.Ar root
and includes nested deeper than eight levels are UNKNOWN.
.Ss banned-lint law
.Bl -tag -width BANNED
.It BANNED
in a
.Pa .c
or
.Pa .h
file,
.Fn gets ,
.Fn strcpy ,
.Fn strcat ,
.Fn sprintf ,
.Fn vsprintf ,
.Fn popen ,
.Fn system
or
.Fn atol :
the name, not part of a longer identifier, followed by
.Ql \&( .
Use
.Xr strlcpy 3 ,
.Xr strlcat 3 ,
.Xr snprintf 3 ,
.Xr strtonum 3
or
.Xr execv 3 .
.El
.Ss want and the controls
.Nm want
runs one case of a gate with standard input from
.Pa /dev/null
under a CPU limit of 60 seconds, names its result and compares it with
.Ar status ,
which is 0, 1 or 2.
With
.Fl l ,
the output must also hold a line that starts with
.Ar law
and a tab.
It prints one line: the kind of result, ok or WRONG, the wanted status
and the command; when WRONG, the command's output follows, indented.
The kinds are PASS, FAIL and UNKNOWN for statuses 0, 1 and 2, SETUP when
the limit could not be set or the command could not run, TIMEOUT when the
CPU limit killed it, KILLED for any other signal, and ERROR.
.Pp
.Ic make check
in the gates directory runs every case, so a wrong result never hides
the cases after it, and exits non-zero if any case was WRONG.
For each gate it runs the valid positives (the gates' own directory and
the green controls), a known-bad control for every law, the
infrastructure failures (a refused registry, a name outside the alphabet,
a tree with nothing to judge and a missing root), and two cases that show
a result reaching its caller: a wrong expectation of a red control must
make
.Nm want
exit 1, and a command killed by a signal must be reported as KILLED, never
as a result of the gate.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The gates exit 0 for PASS, 1 for FAIL and 2 for UNKNOWN, including a
usage error.
.Nm want
exits 0 when the result is the wanted one, 1 when it is not and 2 on a
usage error.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa gates/walk
the walk shared by the three gates
.It Pa gates/foreign.awk , gates/mk.awk
the judging programs, run by
.Xr awk 1
.It Pa root/GATE-FIXTURES
the directories a gate does not walk
.It Pa controls/
the fixtures of every control, by gate
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run every control:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cd gates && make check
.Ed
.Pp
Judge one component, here the controls' own green Makefile:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ sh gates/mk-lint controls/mk/good; echo $?
mk-lint: PASS makefiles=1 failed=0 unknown=0
0
.Ed
.Pp
A known-bad control:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ sh gates/banned-lint controls/banned/red; echo $?
BANNED	controls/banned/red/main.c	7		return strcpy(d, s);
banned-lint: FAIL judged=1 findings=1 unknown=0
1
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr awk 1 ,
.Xr find 1 ,
.Xr make 1 ,
.Xr sh 1 ,
.Xr malloc 3 ,
.Xr style 9
.Sh AUTHORS
